  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Ss5HF839UNqHmDtDTZIP79Yxp2s=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Do not disable SSR for it\n\nThe reflex with anything wallet-adjacent is to wrap it in `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false`, because wallet libraries touch `window`. `RenownProvider` does **not** need that and must not get it: each adapter's wallet library is fetched only on the **first login click**, so the provider itself renders on the server unchanged.\n\nWrapping it in `ssr: false` costs you the server-rendered authenticated shell and reintroduces the logged-in flash it is designed to avoid.\n\n```tsx\nimport { RenownProvider } from \"@powerhousedao/reactor-browser/renown\";\nimport { privyAdapter } from \"@renown/sdk/wallet/privy\";\n\n// Module scope: RenownWalletProvider snapshots this array on mount.\nconst adapters = [privyAdapter({ appId: \"...\", methods: [\"google\", \"email\"] })];\n\n<RenownProvider appName=\"my-app\" namespace=\"my-app\"\n  switchboardUrl=\"https://switchboard.example/graphql\" adapters={adapters}>\n  {children}\n</RenownProvider>\n```\n\n## Two first-render strategies\n\n**Client-only apps** (Vite and similar): the provider seeds the first render **synchronously from `localStorage`**, so a returning user is authenticated on the first paint with no flash.\n\n**SSR apps** (Next.js): pass a server-resolved `session`, read from a verified session cookie in a Data Access Layer. Under SSR the cookie seeds the server render and hydration \u2014 it is the only thing readable server-side \u2014 and then `localStorage` takes over once mounted, since that is the credential the SDK actually restores. Passing `session` also keeps the cookie in sync after login and logout.\n\nBecause two sources feed the same UI, include the `documentId`/`username`/`userImage` fields in the cookie's profile hint so both agree on name, avatar and profile links.\n\n## Gating on auth\n\nUse a plain `if (!user)` from `useRenownAuth()`. For a no-Suspense \"still resolving\" state, `useRenownAuthAsync()` returns `state: \"authenticated\" | \"resolving\" | \"unauthenticated\"`. `\"resolving\"` appears only when the answer is genuinely unknown \u2014 a visitor the first render already knows is signed out resolves straight to `\"unauthenticated\"`, so logged-out visitors never sit behind a spinner.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/07-Authorization/01-RenownAuthenticationFlow.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z"
    }
  },
